      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "10da3200-a880-58ad-a14b-d3b641bac2fb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: 300 Entertainment\n- People: Fetty Wap, Raz Simone, Tee Grizzley, Young Thug, Shy Glizzy, Rejjie Snow, Alex Winston, Migos, Conrad Sewell, Highly Suspect, Cobi, Meg Mac, Dae Dae, Coheed and Cambria, ASTR, Tate Kobang, Mainland, Maggie Lindemann, Famous Dex, Cheat Codes, The Hunna, Bailey Bryan, Demo Taped, Creek Boyz, OMB Peezy, Natalie La Rose, Marco \"MAG\" Borrero, Ilya Salmanzadeh, Max Martin, Savan Kotecha, Rickard Goransson, DJ Frank E\n- Songs: \"Trap Queen\", \"Nasty Freestyle\", \"Around the World\"\n- Charts: Billboard Hot 100, Bubbling Under Hot 100 Singles\n\nFacts:\n- On May 4, 2015, \"Nasty Freestyle\" was released as a digital download in the United States by 300 Entertainment.\n- In May 2015, Fetty Wap rose to prominence after his debut single \"Trap Queen\" reached number two on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100.\n- \"Nasty Freestyle\" became a commercial success and peaked at number nine on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100.\n- \"Around the World\" by Natalie La Rose features American rapper Fetty Wap.\n- Fetty Wap co-wrote \"Around the World\" with producers Marco \"MAG\" Borrero, Ilya Salmanzadeh, and Max Martin, and the song also has additional writing from Savan Kotecha, Rickard Goransson, and DJ Frank E.\n- \"Around the World\" reached number 3 on the U.S. Billboard Bubbling Under Hot 100 Singles chart.\n- 300 Entertainment's label roster includes Raz Simone, Tee Grizzley, Fetty Wap, Young Thug, Shy Glizzy, Rejjie Snow, Alex Winston, Migos, Conrad Sewell, Highly Suspect, Cobi, Meg Mac, Dae Dae, Coheed and Cambria, ASTR, Tate Kobang, Mainland, Maggie Lindemann, Famous Dex, Cheat Codes, The Hunna, Bailey Bryan, Demo Taped, Creek Boyz, and OMB Peezy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7f9abd0c-05ce-5073-93d5-6d8d790a04f1",
        "text": "Page: 300 Entertainment. Sentence: The label currently includes Raz Simone, Tee Grizzley, Fetty Wap, Young Thug, Shy Glizzy, Rejjie Snow, Alex Winston, Migos, Conrad Sewell, Highly Suspect, Cobi, Meg Mac, Dae Dae, Coheed and Cambria, ASTR, Tate Kobang, Mainland, Maggie Lindemann, Famous Dex, Cheat Codes, The Hunna, Bailey Bryan, Demo Taped, Creek Boyz, and OMB Peezy.\nPage: Fetty Wap. Sentence: He rose to prominence after his debut single \"Trap Queen\", reached number two on the U.S. \"Billboard\" Hot 100 chart in May 2015.\nPage: Nasty Freestyle. Sentence: Released as a digital download in the United States by 300 Entertainment on May 4, 2015, it soon became a commercial success, peaking at number nine on the US \"Billboard\" Hot 100.\nPage: Around the World (Natalie La Rose song). Sentence: It features American rapper Fetty Wap, who co-wrote the song with its producers Marco \"MAG\" Borrero, Ilya Salmanzadeh, and Max Martin, with additional writing from Savan Kotecha, Rickard Goransson, and DJ Frank E.\nPage: Around the World (Natalie La Rose song). Sentence: The single reached number 3 on the US \"Billboard\" Bubbling Under Hot 100 Singles chart.",
